# Playwright E2E & Browser Forensic Audit Rules
- Prefer user-facing locators (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByText`) over brittle CSS/XPath chains.
- Never use arbitrary `waitForTimeout` sleeps when an assertion or network response wait (`expect(...).toBeVisible()`) expresses the true readiness condition.
- Capture real failed HTTP `4xx/5xx` responses separately from intentional lazy-loaded below-the-fold images (`loading="lazy"`).
- Always close browser contexts cleanly inside `try { ... } finally { await browser.close(); }`.
